  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Eleven on the move – non-stop 3v2",
  "description": "Eleven players, full court. At each basket two defenders wait, one at the free-throw line and one under the basket. At each half there are also two outlet players, one on each sideline at free-throw-line height. The last three players attack 3v2 at one end.\n\nWhen the attack is over – basket, rebound or turnover – one of the defenders takes the ball (inbounding from the baseline after a make) and passes to one of the outlets. The passer and both outlet players become the new attackers and go 3v2 to the other end. Two of the old attackers stay as the new defenders, and the third attacker and the other defender take the outlet spots. The drill never stops.\n\nProgression: keep score and add a time limit, for example seven seconds per attack. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attack: ball in the middle, wings wide – finish fast with one or two passes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Defence: the top defender stops the ball, the back defender takes the first pass. Talk all the time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Secure the rebound and look straight for the outlet – the first pass starts the next attack."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Outlets are ready with hands up and sprint away the moment they catch."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
